From 7eb8b618adf7e2a1d4fed1e4170f2e3301af2519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 16:33:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): trim 17 over-cap descriptions to <=1024 chars
 (Phase A #1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the regression from #292: 17/19 skill descriptions exceeded the 1024-char
Anthropic Agent Skills spec limit. A multi-agent trim pass (trim -> adversarial
verify) rewrote each to <=996 chars while preserving the pushy "use this when..."
triggering and the sibling-discrimination NOT-blocks that keep queries routing to
exactly one skill. Every skill is now under the cap (max 996); per-skill verify
confirmed discrimination + pushiness preserved for all 17. .codex mirror inSync.

Refs strategy docs/work/2026-07-05-efficiency-extensibility-strategy §P1; kernel
issue 258725e8 (Phase A #1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
